{"event":"result","result":{"conversation_id":"99e474f7-96e1-4670-b07d-1cff55e89b9c","status":"SUCCESS","response":"The cause of the issue has been diagnosed and fixed, and the full explanation is documented in [ANSWER.md](file:///tmp/h-1OcNXu/ANSWER.md).\n\n### Summary of Causes \u0026 Fixes\n\n1. **Why Telegram never received anything (not even a failure notification):**\n   - In [`bin/nightly-review.zsh`](file:///tmp/h-1OcNXu/bin/nightly-review.zsh#L19), line 19 assigned `status=$?`.\n   - In `zsh`, `status` is a built-in read-only variable aliasing `$?`. Attempting to assign to `status` caused a fatal error (`read-only variable: status`), immediately terminating the script before it could evaluate the exit code or call [`bin/notify.sh`](file:///tmp/h-1OcNXu/bin/notify.sh).\n   - **Fix:** Renamed `status` to `exit_code` in [`bin/nightly-review.zsh`](file:///tmp/h-1OcNXu/bin/nightly-review.zsh).\n\n2. **Why the review command failed (`Not logged in · Please run /login`):**\n   - `launchd` executes jobs without standard interactive environment variables such as `USER`.\n   - Claude Code queries the macOS Keychain for credentials under account `process.env.USER`. When unset, it fell back to querying account `\"claude-code-user\"` rather than the user's account name.\n   - **Fix:** Added `USER` (`vk`) to `EnvironmentVariables` in [`Library/LaunchAgents/com.vk.nightly-review.plist`](file:///tmp/h-1OcNXu/Library/LaunchAgents/com.vk.nightly-review.plist#L24-L28).\n","duration_seconds":467.00298,"num_turns":1,"usage":{"input_tokens":297144,"output_tokens":12180,"thinking_tokens":0,"cache_read_tokens":3371509,"total_tokens":309324}}}
